SUMMARY:Deadline 17:00 CET: European Cultural Foundation: ERASMUS 40 Creati
 ve Research Fellowship (Florence archives\, Brussels presentation)
DESCRIPTION:Closes 01 Dec 2026 at 17:00 CET.\n\nTo mark the 40th anniversar
 y of ERASMUS in 2027\, the European Cultural Foundation is opening its his
 torical archives for a Creative Research Fellowship: one professional crea
 tive practitioner will research ECF's lesser-known role in shaping the ERA
 SMUS student mobility programme (from the European Institute of Education 
 and the Office for Cooperation in Education to the ERASMUS Bureau\, which 
 ran...\n\nOrganisation: European Cultural Foundation (ECF)\, with the Hist
 orical Archives of the European Union (EUI) and the House of European Hist
 ory\nLocation: Research stay in Florence\, Italy (Historical Archives of t
 he EU) in the first trimester of 2027\; final work presented in Brussels i
 n September 2027. Open to creative practitioners residing in a Council of 
 Europe member state.\nAward: EUR 10\,000 grant covering travel\, living ex
 penses and artistic production. One fellowship.\nDuration: Research reside
 ncy in Florence in the first trimester of 2027 (January to March)\; presen
 tation in September 2027\n\nMore: https://culturalfoundation.eu/open-calls
 /erasmus-fellowship-call/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium
 =referral
URL:https://culturalfoundation.eu/open-calls/erasmus-fellowship-call/?utm_s
 ource=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Research stay in Florence\, Italy (Historical Archives of the EU) 
 in the first trimester of 2027\; final work presented in Brussels in Septe
 mber 2027. Open to creative practitioners residing in a Council of Europe 
 member state.
END:VEVENT
