SUMMARY:Deadline 23:59 EST: USHMM Simon-Skjodt Center: Genocide and Atrocit
 y Prevention Research Fellowship 2027-28 (USD 20\,000-30\,000)
DESCRIPTION:Closes 13 Dec 2026 at 23:59 EST.\n\nThe Simon-Skjodt Center fun
 ds policy-relevant research on preventing genocide and mass atrocities\, f
 rom any discipline. Fellows work non-residentially for a year and present 
 at a workshop in Washington\, DC. ELIGIBILITY: enrolled PhD students or re
 searchers within 5 years of completing a PhD\, any nationality\, any disci
 pline. APPLY via the Smartsheet form linked from the fellowship page.\n\nO
 rganisation: United States Holocaust Memorial Museum\, Simon-Skjodt Center
  for the Prevention of Genocide\nLocation: Non-residential\, worldwide\; o
 ne workshop in Washington\, DC (travel covered).\nAward: USD 20\,000 for P
 hD students\; USD 30\,000 for researchers within 5 years of their PhD\; pl
 us travel to one Washington DC workshop. No application fee stated.\nDurat
 ion: 1 June 2027 to 31 May 2028\n\nMore: https://www.ushmm.org/genocide-pr
 evention/simon-skjodt-center/work/research/genocide-and-atrocity-preventio
 n-research-fellowship?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=ref
 erral
URL:https://www.ushmm.org/genocide-prevention/simon-skjodt-center/work/rese
 arch/genocide-and-atrocity-prevention-research-fellowship?utm_source=artif
 icialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Non-residential\, worldwide\; one workshop in Washington\, DC (tra
 vel covered).
END:VEVENT
